{"timestamp":1774885706961,"source_app":"agentic-harness","session_id":"a7a57b23-3635-4f41-9593-e2cd117f9072","hook_event_type":"PreToolUse","tool_name":"Write","tool_use_id":"toolu_01CqZb98TYuCQktqtCBUoYrZ","payload":{"session_id":"a7a57b23-3635-4f41-9593-e2cd117f9072","transcript_path":"/Users/rivero/.claude/projects/-Users-rivero-ai-agentic-experience-apps-mas-trees-1623864e/a7a57b23-3635-4f41-9593-e2cd117f9072.jsonl","cwd":"/Users/rivero/ai/agentic-experience/apps/mas/trees/1623864e","permission_mode":"bypassPermissions","hook_event_name":"PreToolUse","tool_name":"Write","tool_input":{"file_path":"/Users/rivero/ai/agentic-experience/apps/mas/trees/1623864e/specs/patch/patch-adw-11-fix-deduplicate-test-assertion.md","content":"# Patch: Fix deduplication test to assert saveCall.called unconditionally\n\n## Metadata\nadw_id: `11`\nreview_change_request: `Issue #2: Deduplication test uses 'if (saveCall.called) { expect } else { expect.fail }' instead of asserting saveCall.called unconditionally. Functionally correct but reduces test clarity and CI output readability. Resolution: Replace with expect(saveCall.called).to.be.true; then assert savedFragment.title unconditionally. Severity: tech_debt`\n\n## Issue Summary\n**Original Spec:** N/A\n**Issue:** The `'deduplicates title when it already exists in the folder'` test wraps its core assertions in an `if (saveCall.called)` branch with a matching `else { expect.fail(...) }`. This is functionally equivalent but produces less readable CI output and obscures intent \u2014 Mocha/Chai will not identify which assertion failed as clearly.\n**Solution:** Replace the conditional block with `expect(saveCall.called).to.be.true;` followed by unconditional extraction of `saveCall.firstCall.args[0]` and assertion on its `title`.\n\n## Files to Modify\n\n- `studio/test/mas-repository.test.js` \u2014 lines 1535\u20131543\n\n## Implementation Steps\nIMPORTANT: Execute every step in order, top to bottom.\n\n### Step 1: Replace the conditional assertion block with unconditional assertions\nIn `studio/test/mas-repository.test.js`, locate the block at lines 1535\u20131543:\n\n```js\nconst saveCall = repo.aem.sites.cf.fragments.save;\nif (saveCall.called) {\n    const savedFragment = saveCall.firstCall.args[0];\n    expect(savedFragment.title).to.equal('lucy-card-1');\n} else {\n    // save was not called means uniqueTitle === result.title; that means\n    // deduplication didn't trigger \u2014 which would be a bug.\n    expect.fail('save should have been called with the deduplicated title');\n}\n```\n\nReplace it with:\n\n```js\nconst saveCall = repo.aem.sites.cf.fragments.save;\nexpect(saveCall.called).to.be.true;\nconst savedFragment = saveCall.firstCall.args[0];\nexpect(savedFragment.title).to.equal('lucy-card-1');\n```\n\n## Validation\nExecute every command to validate the patch is complete with zero regressions.\n\n1. Verify JS syntax: `node --check studio/test/mas-repository.test.js`\n2. Run the relevant test suite: `npm run test:unit -- --grep \"deduplicates title\"` (or equivalent mocha command in the project)\n3. Confirm no `if (saveCall.called)` pattern remains in the file: `grep -n \"if (saveCall.called)\" studio/test/mas-repository.test.js` \u2014 should return no output\n\n## Patch Scope\n**Lines of code to change:** ~7 lines removed, ~3 lines added (net -4)\n**Risk level:** low\n**Testing required:** Run the single unit test `'deduplicates title when it already exists in the folder'` and confirm it passes with a clear assertion error message on failure\n"},"tool_use_id":"toolu_01CqZb98TYuCQktqtCBUoYrZ"}}
